@nsobid-646761F643AFEBB379EDD5E6A5151AF2CEF93DC1

# Metroid Dread 2.1.0 - Disable FXAA

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Disables the FXAA post-process pass (the "pp_fxaa" effect).
//
// The final post chain first runs a plain copy pass into the output target
// (sub_71001DBA58), then, when docked, re-renders the same target from the same
// source through FXAA (sub_71001DBE3C). Dropping that call leaves the plain
// copy in place, so the presented image is identical minus the blur. Handheld
// never runs FXAA, so it is unaffected either way.

@enabled
001DACF8 1F2003D5   // NOP (was BL sub_71001DBE3C = FXAA draw)
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against Metroid Dread 2.1.0 (MercurySteam engine,
// NVN). The retail build is symbol-stripped; every site was located by
// structure and byte-verified against the IDB before being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
